### 3. Proof walker — `fetchUpgrade` → `findPendingAttestation`
**`packages/backend/src/api/crypto/upgrade-helper.ts:37–67`**

```ts
async function fetchUpgrade(inputHashHex, pendingProofHex, logContext) {
    const pending = await findPendingAttestation(inputHashHex, pendingProofHex);
    // pending = { commitmentHex, calendarUrl, prefixLength } | null
    const upgraded = await pollAnyCalendar(pending.commitmentHex, pending.calendarUrl);
    if (!upgraded) return { kind: "still_pending" };
    const splicedHex = spliceUpgrade(pendingProofHex, pending.prefixLength, upgraded);
    return { kind: "upgraded", splicedHex };
}
```

`findPendingAttestation` (`packages/backend/src/lib/ots-proof-walk.ts:67–125`) walks the raw OTS binary proof op-by-op (APPEND, PREPEND, SHA256…), accumulating the intermediate hash. When it hits the `0x00` attestation marker followed by `PENDING_TAG` (`0x83df…8e`), it returns:
- `commitmentHex` — the hash at that point in the chain (what the calendar indexes by)
- `calendarUrl` — the URL embedded in the pending-attestation payload
- `prefixLength` — byte offset of the `0x00` marker (used for splicing later)

